The AI agent must exclusively use `cmake --build ./build` (with the current working directory set to the project root) to compile the project after source-only code modifications. Treat `./build` as the active build tree for the current checkout/worktree; another host, container, WSL, or OS development environment must use another worktree. Unless the human explicitly authorizes a bootstrap/configuration task in the current conversation, the agent must not reconfigure, clean, install, regenerate, delete, move, or recreate build/toolchain outputs, and must not edit CMake/bootstrap/LLVM toolchain definition files that can cause a full or partial rebootstrap. Bash scripts in the project directory are strictly reserved for human developers and must never be executed by the AI agent under any circumstances. Adhere to this directive without exception to maintain build consistency and avoid unintended side effects.
